    "q_en": "Ram's income is $2.5\\%$ more than Shyam's income. By what percent is Shyam's income less than Ram's income?",
    "q_hi": "राम की आय श्याम की आय से $2.5\\%$ अधिक है। श्याम की आय राम की आय से कितने प्रतिशत कम है?",
    "options": ["1.43%", "4.43%", "2.43%", "3.43%"],
    "answer": 2,
    "solution": "$2.5\\% = \\frac{1}{40}$. Let Shyam's income $= 40$, then Ram's income $= 41$.<br>Required less % $= \\frac{41 - 40}{41} \\times 100 = \\frac{100}{41} \\approx 2.43\\%$.",
    "trick": "AB Rule: $+\\frac{1}{40}$ se wapas aane par $-\\frac{1}{41} \\approx 2.43\\%$."
